---
import FAQAccordion from '../components/FAQAccordion.astro';
import Layout from '../components/Layout.astro';
import Button from '../components/ui/Button.astro';
import Card from '../components/ui/Card.astro';
import Heading from '../components/ui/Heading.astro';
import Section from '../components/ui/Section.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';

const faqItems = [
  {
    question: 'How much does a typical website cost?',
    answer:
      'Professional website projects start at $2,900. Final pricing depends on scope, content, functionality, and project requirements.'
  },
  {
    question: 'How do you price custom business applications?',
    answer:
      'Business applications are priced after understanding the workflow, functionality, integrations, users, and overall complexity involved.'
  },
  {
    question: "Why don't business applications have a starting price?",
    answer:
      "A customer contact tool for five employees and a multi-step application with integrations, permissions, and automation are very different projects. I price business applications after understanding the workflow so you're paying for what the business actually needs."
  },
  {
    question: 'Do I need to know exactly what I need before contacting you?',
    answer:
      'No. You can describe the problem, current process, or outcome you want. I can help determine whether the practical solution is a website, business application, integration, automation, or something simpler.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Can we start small and add features later?',
    answer:
      'Yes, when technically practical. A focused first phase is often better than building a large system before the business knows what it actually needs.'
  },
  {
    question: 'What does ongoing support cover?',
    answer:
      'Ongoing support can include website and content updates, minor improvements, reliability and performance checks, troubleshooting, hosting guidance, and planned improvements. Basic website support starts at $250/month. Support for custom business applications or more involved systems is scoped separately.'
  }
];
---

<Layout
  title="Pricing | Geek Life Development"
  description="Clear pricing for professional websites, custom-scoped business applications, and ongoing support from Geek Life Development."
>
  <Section class="!py-16 md:!py-20">
    <div class="max-w-4xl space-y-6">
      <p class="label-mono text-slate-500">PRICING</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl leading-tight md:text-6xl">Clear pricing where it makes sense. Custom quotes where it doesn't.</h1>
      <p class="max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-neutral)] md:text-lg">
        Some projects are straightforward enough to have a starting price. Others depend on the workflow, integrations, and business problem being solved. Either way, we'll define the scope and cost before development begins.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <Button href="/contact" size="lg">Get a quote</Button>
        <Button href={siteConfig.phoneHref} size="lg" variant="secondary">Talk through your project</Button>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">
        Prefer to talk first? <a href={siteConfig.phoneHref} class="font-medium">Call or text {siteConfig.phoneDisplay}</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">Serving Ozaukee County & the Milwaukee area + remote.</p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section variant="muted" class="!py-14 md:!py-16">
    <div class="space-y-8">
      <Heading
        eyebrow="HOW PRICING WORKS"
        title="Start with the problem. Define the scope. Know the cost before we build."
        subtitle="Every project starts by understanding what you're trying to accomplish. From there, I'll recommend the simplest practical approach and define the scope, timeline, and investment before development begins."
      />

      <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
        <Card hover={false} class="p-5">
          <p class="label-mono text-slate-500">01</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Understand the need</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">We talk through the business problem, goals, users, and current process.</p>
        </Card>
        <Card hover={false} class="p-5">
          <p class="label-mono text-slate-500">02</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Define the solution</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">I recommend the right approach and establish the project scope.</p>
        </Card>
        <Card hover={false} class="p-5">
          <p class="label-mono text-slate-500">03</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Approve before building</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">You receive a clear scope, timeline, and price before development begins.</p>
        </Card>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section class="!py-14 md:!py-16">
    <div class="space-y-10">
      <Heading
        eyebrow="SERVICE PRICING"
        title="Three ways to work together"
        subtitle="Straightforward projects have useful starting prices. Custom work is scoped around the business problem and defined before development begins."
      />

      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-3">
        <Card class="h-full">
          <p class="label-mono text-slate-500">PROFESSIONAL WEBSITES</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Professional Websites</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Starting at $2,900</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-600">For small businesses that need a professional, modern website that clearly explains what they do and turns visitors into inquiries.</p>
          <p class="mt-5 label-mono text-slate-500">Typical projects can include</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-700">
            <li>• Clear site structure and messaging</li>
            <li>• Responsive design</li>
            <li>• Contact or lead-generation forms</li>
            <li>• Search-friendly technical setup</li>
            <li>• Launch and post-launch support</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-700"><strong>Typical timeline:</strong> approximately 1–3 weeks depending on scope.</p>
          <Button href="/contact" class="mt-6 w-full">Discuss a website</Button>
        </Card>

        <Card class="h-full border-blue-200/80 bg-blue-50/30">
          <p class="label-mono text-slate-500">BUSINESS APPLICATIONS</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Custom Business Applications</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Pricing based on scope</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600">Business applications are priced around the workflow, complexity, integrations, and functionality required.</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-600">For businesses that need a focused tool to replace spreadsheets, repetitive work, disconnected processes, or awkward manual workflows.</p>
          <p class="mt-5 label-mono text-slate-500">Examples can include</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-700">
            <li>• Customer or contact management</li>
            <li>• Scheduling and workflow tools</li>
            <li>• Forms and data collection</li>
            <li>• Internal dashboards</li>
            <li>• Member or volunteer management</li>
            <li>• Process automation</li>
            <li>• Connected website-to-office workflows</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-slate-800">You do not need to know what software you need before reaching out.</p>
          <Button href="/contact" class="mt-6 w-full">Discuss a business problem</Button>
        </Card>

        <Card class="h-full">
          <p class="label-mono text-slate-500">ONGOING SUPPORT</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Ongoing Support</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Starting at $250/month</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-600">For straightforward websites that need dependable maintenance, updates, and ongoing attention.</p>
          <p class="mt-5 label-mono text-slate-500">Typical support can include</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-700">
            <li>• Content and data updates</li>
            <li>• Small layout or usability improvements</li>
            <li>• Reliability and performance checks</li>
            <li>• Troubleshooting</li>
            <li>• Minor workflow improvements</li>
            <li>• Hosting and deployment guidance</li>
            <li>• Planned improvements as priorities change</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-700">Support for business applications, more active websites, or systems with more involved monthly needs is scoped based on complexity and expected support.</p>
          <Button href="/services#ongoing-support" class="mt-6 w-full">Explore ongoing support</Button>
        </Card>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section variant="muted" class="!py-14 md:!py-16">
    <div class="grid items-start gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[1.05fr_0.95fr]">
      <Heading
        eyebrow="FLEXIBLE SCOPE"
        title="Some projects need more than one piece."
        subtitle="A project might begin with a website and later add an internal business application. Or the website may act as the front door to a workflow your team manages behind the scenes."
      />

      <Card hover={false}>
        <p class="label-mono text-slate-500">Example flow</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm font-medium text-slate-900 md:text-base">Website → Form or Customer Action → Business Application → Team Workflow</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-600">We'll scope the pieces that make sense now without forcing you to build everything at once.</p>
      </Card>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section class="!py-14 md:!py-16">
    <div class="space-y-8">
      <Heading
        eyebrow="SCOPE & COMPLEXITY"
        title="What affects project pricing?"
      />

      <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        <Card hover={false} class="p-5">
          <p class="font-medium text-slate-900">Number of pages or screens</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">More content, views, or workflows require additional design and development.</p>
        </Card>
        <Card hover={false} class="p-5">
          <p class="font-medium text-slate-900">Custom functionality</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">Unique business rules or interactions increase development scope.</p>
        </Card>
        <Card hover={false} class="p-5">
          <p class="font-medium text-slate-900">Integrations</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">Connecting payment systems, calendars, email, APIs, or existing tools adds implementation and testing.</p>
        </Card>
        <Card hover={false} class="p-5">
          <p class="font-medium text-slate-900">Content and data</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">Migration, content entry, cleanup, or structured data can affect scope.</p>
        </Card>
        <Card hover={false} class="p-5">
          <p class="font-medium text-slate-900">Workflow complexity</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">Multi-step processes, permissions, notifications, and automation require additional planning and development.</p>
        </Card>
        <Card hover={false} class="p-5">
          <p class="font-medium text-slate-900">Ongoing needs</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">Support, maintenance, hosting, and planned improvements are scoped around how the system will be used.</p>
        </Card>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">The goal isn't to make the project bigger. It's to identify what you actually need and price that clearly.</p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section variant="muted" class="!py-14 md:!py-16">
    <div class="max-w-4xl">
      <Card hover={false} class="border-sky-100 bg-sky-50/80 px-6 py-7 md:px-8 md:py-8">
        <p class="label-mono text-slate-500">START SMALL</p>
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Custom software doesn't have to mean a massive project.</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700 md:text-base">Often the best first step is solving one high-value problem — replacing a spreadsheet, simplifying an intake process, organizing customer information, or removing repetitive work. Additional functionality can be added later when it makes sense.</p>
      </Card>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section class="!py-14 md:!py-16">
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.2fr]">
      <Heading
        eyebrow="FAQ"
        title="Common pricing questions"
        subtitle="Concise answers to help you understand pricing and next steps."
      />
      <FAQAccordion items={faqItems} />
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section variant="dark">
    <div class="space-y-6 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-white">Have a project in mind — or just a problem that needs solving?</h2>
      <p class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-slate-300">Tell me what you're trying to accomplish. I'll help determine the practical next step and what it is likely to cost.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3">
        <Button href="/contact" size="lg">Get a quote</Button>
        <Button href={siteConfig.phoneHref} size="lg" variant="secondary">Talk through your project</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Layout>